From 76c65f277f7d74e54666f4ffaf1244f93e25693e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan Hertenberger <erde74@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 15:19:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] syscall: plan9: rc's functions and the wait message as
 Plan 9 has them

A child's /env got every value with a NUL after it: right for a variable (a
list, each word ended by a NUL), but a function (fn#name) is rc source that
rc reads back with ". -bq", and the NUL made it a syntax error in every rc
started from Go ("/env/fn#sigexit:1: syntax error"). envValue writes both as
rc does, for fork/exec and for Exec alike (Exec wrote no NUL at all); an
empty function (rc leaves /env/fn#x empty after fn x) is written as 0 bytes
from a valid address, as the kernel refuses nil even then.

Waitmsg.Msg kept the kernel's %q quoting ('rc 123: it''s'; only '' was
taken out): it is now the message itself, as libc's wait gives it, and
ExitError.Error() says "exit status: rc 123: it's". TestExitStatus expected
the quotes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
